    "issue_context": {
        "number": 110753,
        "title": "LogsDB - Support `doc_values: false` for all field types",
        "body": "### Description\n\nThe following two PRs:\r\n* https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/110016\r\n* https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/110160\r\n\r\naddress supporting synthetic source when doc values are disabled for numeric and keyword fields. We identified those two types to be the most used in mappings with disabled doc values. We need, anyway, to extend support for all field types so that we can reconstruct documents source even if doc values are disabled. Under the hood, when `doc_values: false` we just use a stored field to save the field contents and use it at document reconstruction time.",
        "comments": [
            "Pinging @elastic/es-storage-engine (Team:StorageEngine)"
        ]
    },
